### Before the kernel is initialised, for the LYSO panel's own radioactivity (macro/muonic_xray_lyso.mac):
###   ./TOFmeter --preinit macro/preinit_lyso.mac <macro>
### Geant4's radioactive decay, for the Lu-176 of the LYSO (/tof/intrinsic/). It also turns on fluorescence and Auger
### electrons (and deexcitation below the production cuts) in every volume, so that X-rays such as Lu's K X-rays come out
### (the K-escape of photons above the Lu K edge, 63.3 keV: Al L-alpha 65.7 keV, Si 76.2 keV). The CZT runs have them off.
### macro/muonic_xray_lyso.mac and lyso_decay_only.mac turn the Auger electrons off again after the initialisation
### (/process/em/auger false: their energy stays in the pixel anyway, and the run is 1.5 times as fast).

/tof/physics/radioactiveDecay
/process/em/fluo true
